  "claim": "The album supported by The Who Tour 2000 was an album by The Who that can still be found on eBay Inc., an e-commerce platform that was founded in the 90's.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Blues to the Bush. Sentence: Blues to the Bush is a live album by The Who recorded at the House of Blues in Chicago on 12 and 13 November 1999, and at the Empire Theatre, Shepherd's Bush on 22 and 23 December 1999.\nPage: Blues to the Bush. Sentence: It was sold exclusively from the now defunct MusicMaker.com, though it can still be found on torrent sites and second hand markets such as EBay.\nPage: EBay. Sentence: eBay Inc. ( , stylized as ebay) is a multinational e-commerce corporation, facilitating online consumer-to-consumer and business-to-consumer sales.\nPage: EBay. Sentence: eBay was founded by Pierre Omidyar in 1995, and became a notable success story of the dot-com bubble.\nPage: The Who Tour 2000. Sentence: The Who Tour 2000 was partially in support of The Who's live album \"The Blues to the Bush\" and their first full-fledged tour as a five-piece band since The Who Tour 1982.",
