        "original_id": "8751e03b-133a-526a-a4fe-e82801fdfce5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Blues to the Bush\n- People: The Who, Pierre Omidyar\n- Companies: MusicMaker.com, eBay Inc.\n- Places: House of Blues in Chicago, Empire Theatre Shepherd's Bush\n- Events: The Who Tour 2000, The Who Tour 1982\n- Topics: live albums, e-commerce, dot-com bubble\n\nFacts:\n- eBay Inc. was founded by Pierre Omidyar in 1995 and became a notable success story of the dot-com bubble.\n- Blues to the Bush is a live album by The Who recorded at the House of Blues in Chicago on 12 and 13 November 1999 and at the Empire Theatre in Shepherd's Bush on 22 and 23 December 1999.\n- Blues to the Bush was sold exclusively through the now defunct MusicMaker.com, and it can still be found on torrent sites and second-hand markets such as eBay.\n- The Who Tour 2000 was partially in support of Blues to the Bush and was The Who's first full-fledged tour as a five-piece band since The Who Tour 1982.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
